WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.585
If you are a credentialed non-arts teacher

2
00:00:02.585 --> 00:00:04.254
and you want to teach the arts,

3
00:00:04.254 --> 00:00:07.882
One pathway is to add a supplementary authorization

4
00:00:07.882 --> 00:00:09.259
to your existing credential.

5
00:00:09.259 --> 00:00:11.302
For mutiple subject credential holders,

6
00:00:11.302 --> 00:00:13.930
adding a supplementary authorization

7
00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:15.432
allows you to teach the arts

8
00:00:15.432 --> 00:00:17.517
in grade nine and below.

9
00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:19.561
You'll need 20 semester units,

10
00:00:19.561 --> 00:00:22.022
or 10 upper division semester units

11
00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:23.690
in the content area.

12
00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:24.941
For example,

13
00:00:24.941 --> 00:00:26.234
a dance authorization

14
00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:27.527
must include classes

15
00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:29.279
from the dance department,

16
00:00:29.279 --> 00:00:30.572
and only units from

17
00:00:30.572 --> 00:00:33.366
institutions of higher education are allowed.

18
00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:34.492
The advantage is,

19
00:00:34.492 --> 00:00:36.870
you don't need any classes or exams,

20
00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:40.665
and the application is made directly to the CTC.

21
00:00:40.665 --> 00:00:42.667
For single-subject credential holders,

22
00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:44.294
you can follow the same process

23
00:00:44.294 --> 00:00:48.006
to add a specific supplementary authorization

24
00:00:48.006 --> 00:00:49.799
Or if you choose, you can add

25
00:00:49.799 --> 00:00:51.801
a second single subject
credential

26
00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:54.763
by demonstrating subject matter competency

27
00:00:54.763 --> 00:00:57.724
and taking a one-semester methods course

28
00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:59.726
in an approved teacher
education program.

29
00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:01.978
You can prove subject matter
competency

30
00:01:01.978 --> 00:01:05.523
through a degree in dance, music, theatre,

31
00:01:05.523 --> 00:01:07.233
or visual arts,

32
00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:08.568
by taking the CSET,

33
00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:11.446
or through a combination of college coursework

34
00:01:11.446 --> 00:01:12.947
and one CSET.

35
00:01:12.947 --> 00:01:14.324
So how do you begin?

36
00:01:14.324 --> 00:01:15.658
Review your transcripts

37
00:01:15.658 --> 00:01:17.619
and consult the CTC website

38
00:01:17.619 --> 00:01:19.204
for specific information

39
00:01:19.204 --> 00:01:22.373
regarding supplementary authorizations.

40
00:01:22.373 --> 00:01:24.584
Because individual
circumstances can vary

41
00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:26.461
and there are some limitations

42
00:01:26.461 --> 00:01:28.546
on what subjects can be taught,

43
00:01:28.546 --> 00:01:31.174
we recommend reviewing the CTC guidance

44
00:01:31.174 --> 00:01:33.384
and contacting the Commission directly

45
00:01:33.384 --> 00:01:34.969
with specific questions.

46
00:01:34.969 --> 00:01:37.013
In general though, the process

47
00:01:37.013 --> 00:01:40.016
is more straightforward
than you might think.
